    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are looking at an explosive offensive slate today, headlined by three premier plays: **Trea Turner** (81.27), **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), and **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42). **Trea Turner** sits at the top of our rankings as he faces Andrew Abbott; the combination of a favorable 5.07 xERA matchup and a prime leadoff spot gives him an elite floor. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a must-start, benefiting from a massive +16% park adjustment and a 100% stolen base opportunity rate against Shane Baz\u2019s slow delivery. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** does carry a 44% rain risk warning, his massive upside in our scarcest category\u2014stolen bases\u2014makes him an essential anchor. **Kyle Schwarber** rounds out the top trio, leveraging his dynamic platoon advantage against the lefty Abbott to provide high-ceiling power production.\n\nWe continue to prioritize high-efficiency matchups elsewhere, specifically with **Christian Yelich** (70.70), who gains significant value from a +13% platoon boost. Our most difficult lineup decision was keeping **Josh Smith** (49.83) on the bench. He was the highest-rated reserve, nearly cracking the lineup on the strength of a +14% platoon edge against Jos\u00e9 Soriano; however, the optimizer ultimately favored the superior order positioning of **Dillon Dingler** and **Carson Benge**. While **Yordan Alvarez** (49.70) has the lowest score in our starting lineup due to a difficult L/L matchup against Andrew Alvarez, his elite xwOBA of 0.479 provides too much raw output to bench. We remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several players, but with **Colt Keith** (63.93) and **Junior Caminero** (60.79) locked into strong spots, the Zebras are well-positioned to capitalize on these mid-tier pitching matchups.",
